  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The TestParseDate mehtod in the TestDateUtility class assumes that the machine the test are being executed on has its language settings set to English. The last member of of the array dates, shown below, has the English abbreviation \"Thu\" which cant be parsed in other languages. So the DateUtility.parseDateAsUTC returns null when it is actually doing what it is supposed to.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "String[] dates =",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "{\"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z\", \"1970-01-01T00:00:00.00Z\",",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"1970-01-01T00:00:00.0Z\", \"1970-01-01T00:00:00Z\",",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"1970-01-01Z\", \"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000\",",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"1970-01-01T00:00:00.00\", \"1970-01-01T00:00:00.0\",",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"1970-01-01T00:00:00\", \"1970-01-01\",",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"Thu, 01 Jan 1970 00:00:00 GMT\"};",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Solution: Generate the GMT string with Javas Date class. This should insure that the language of the machine doesnt matter in the unittest ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The workaround for this is to set your machines language setting to English",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
